MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Fab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Fab_m01_001: Harvest season must be approaching in Fódlan.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Fab_m01_002: That brings to mind the difference between the\nAdrestian and Dagdan calendars.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Fab_m01_003: Had you noticed? The calendar of this land begins\nwith Janai and ends with Decim.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Fab_m01_004: Fódlan's year begins with the Great Tree Moon, or\nEfraul, and ends with the Lone Moon—Maresh.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Fab_m01_005: Both calendars no doubt had their origins in the\ncalendar used in antiquity.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Fab_m01_006: Yet somehow, they diverged. In Fódlan the month\nafter the spring equinox now begins the year.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Fab_m01_007: As to the origin of this change, I can only speculate.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Fab_m01_008: My supposition is that it could be based on the\nseason when seeds are sown.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Fab_m01_009: Given the importance of agriculture, it could be\nadministrative as well. Crops must be levied.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Fab_m01_010: Perhaps it is strictly cultural, and the old calendar\nwas deemed unsuitable for some reason.
MID_LGA_1DIT_c10_Fab_m01: <BLN>Had you noticed?
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Esm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Esm_m01_001: Humans really are amazing, aren't they? Since we\ngot back from the desert, it's been on my mind again.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Esm_m01_002: Think about it. We launched ships like Nuwa, bigger\nthan cities, right up into the air!
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Esm_m01_003: I wish I could have seen it.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Esm_m01_004: But they got wiped out anyway, no matter how\nincredible they were.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Esm_m01_005: If we want to understand what's going on, we need\nto think about stuff like this.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Esm_m01_006: It's time I started studying. I want to learn all kinds\nof things.
MID_LGA_1DIT_c10_Esm_m01: <BLN>Humans are amazing.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Mic_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Mic_m01_001: It's been a long time now, but I do still think about\nwhat a good-for-nothing my husband was.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Mic_m01_002: Eight years ago, I finally lost my patience with him\nand kicked him out. That was that!
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Mic_m01_003: Since then, I've done the best I can to raise Mu on\nmy own.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Mic_m01_004: Or so I say, but maybe I just haven't been there\nfor her.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Mic_m01_005: I've been so focused on other things... Am I just using\nthat as a justification for being absent?
MID_LGA_1DIT_c10_Mic_m01: <BLN>Where did I go wrong?
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Set_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Set_m01_001: I haven't seen you in a good while. You appear\nunharmed from the looks of it.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Set_m01_002: Don't misunderstand. I am not particularly\nconcerned with your well-being.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_Set_m01_003: I'm only reiterating what I've said before—that I\nam watching you.
MID_LGA_1DIT_c10_Set_m01: <BLN>You appear unharmed.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_B01_m01_001: You're still unharmed. That is such a relief.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_B01_m01_002: For some time, you were nowhere to be found. I...I\nwas so worried!
MID_LGV_1DIT_c10_B01_m01_003: Take this. It may help ensure your victory.
MID_LGA_1DIT_c10_B01_m01: <BLN>I am relieved to see you well.